<h1>Services</h1>
<p class="lede">Four ways to work together — whichever one you need, whenever you're ready.</p>

<p>We quote every project based on its complexity, scope, and estimated time. No public price list, because no two sites are the same.</p>

<div class="prose">
  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>We combine manual auditing with real screen readers — NVDA, JAWS, Windows Narrator, TalkBack on Android — with automated tools like axe. Automation gives a fast first pass; what actually finds the problems that matter to a real user is manual testing, and there are no shortcuts there.</p>
  <p>We work from WCAG 2.2 as the baseline, aligned with EN 301 549 and the European Accessibility Act (EAA), and when a project calls for it, also with ADA and Section 508 in the United States.</p>
  <p>We're not limited to websites: we audit Android apps, PDF and EPUB documents, desktop software, browser extensions — any digital product you use.</p>
  <p>Every report adapts to who's going to read it: a full document with a criteria table, screenshots, and examples; an Excel breakdown if you need full technical detail; or a plain-language version for the rest of your team. We don't stop at flagging the problem — we propose the fix. And the channel stays open after delivery, especially on the full package.</p>

  <h2>Express audit</h2>
  <p>Need to know, right now, where your site stands? Start here. We review the home page and a selection of key links, with direct observations — the fast diagnosis before committing to a bigger project. It doesn't include the full page-by-page report: that's what the site audit adds.</p>
  <div class="placeholder">Still to confirm: the real turnaround for this service. What you gave (2 weeks to a month) seems to match the full package, not this one.</div>

  <h2>Site audit</h2>
  <p>The solid foundation for any real conformance statement. We evaluate against AA as the floor, with AAA suggested wherever it's achievable — page by page, every link, with a full report and criteria table. We close with a call to go through the findings with whoever you want on your team: we handle the functional and screen-reader side, and visual review is covered by the team as well.</p>
  <div class="placeholder">Still to confirm: whether the scope is always the whole site or a negotiated set of representative pages, and the typical turnaround.</div>

  <h2>Full package</h2>
  <p>Everything in the site audit, plus follow-up after delivery, the accessibility statement already drafted, and a discount on a re-test once you implement the changes. If you'd rather not handle it in-house, we also assess and quote remediation: we fix the HTML and ARIA directly, not just flag it.</p>
  <p>Includes a live audit session — 30 minutes to an hour and a half, depending on what there is to show and discuss — with the full report guaranteed regardless of how that session goes. The recording stays private on a YouTube channel; it's published on the site only if the client explicitly authorizes it.</p>

  <h2>Corporate workshop</h2>
  <p>How your team stops repeating the same accessibility mistakes on every new project. In person in Argentina, remote for the rest of the Spanish-speaking countries, adapted to each team.</p>
  <div class="placeholder">Still pending: who it's aimed at (design, development, both), duration and group size, whether it's theoretical, practical, or a mix, and what language it's delivered in.</div>
</div>

<div class="prose">
  <h2>How we work together</h2>
  <p>We work with individual clients and with agencies, with a preference for direct clients. A 50% deposit is due once the contract is signed — in writing or after a video call — with the rest due on delivery. We accept PayPal and bank transfer from Europe, Argentina, or the US. Quotes are in euros for Spain and dollars for the rest of the Americas, with special pricing for Argentina.</p>
</div>

